The artifacts that work for all the monster types are:

Cleaver, Fire brand, Frost brand, Grimtooth, Mjollnir, Snickersnee and
Stormbringer.

They all have hit probability of 5 except Snickersnee (0?) and Grimtooth
(2).
In terms of the raw damage, Mjollnir is the best (24), Excaibur (10) and
Snickersnee (8).  

Grimtooth and Snickersnee are nice, but they aren't my favorites...

Firebrand and Frostbrand gives you the fire resistent and cold resistent
intrinsics, although I wouldn't rely on Firebrand's intrinsic when going
down to hell.  They have "x2" relative damage bonus, so they could do some
hefty damage, when enchanted.

Mjollnir is an awsome weapon to have.  Can kill pretty much anything with
few blows.

Excalibur is one of the most popular ones because it is easy to get.  It is
a very versatile weapon since it defends against drain level attack and it
is rust proof (gained via fountain or becoming the hand of Elbereth).
I haven't used the trick myself, but Excalibur is the only one you can
enchant it to incredible number (like +20?).  Then it should be hard to
beat...

Stormbringer drains level and defends against drain level.  Rustproof if you
are granted to steal the soul for Arioch.  

>Any clues as to which is better?  

It's up to your taste, but...

I like the Stormy best because I think level draining is most effective
against the powerful monsters.  I like the message too.

I sometimes wish for Mojo (I don't play lawful) because of its sheer
power ONLY IF I have Excalibur (which I usually do).  I need a way to
defend against level draining (God, I hate that!)

>And if you repeatedly use Stormbringer, are
